# Bedrock repo-local @context — the single serviceable context for every
# situation/<ns>/ vertex (SPINE §4 C3: one @context, no remote loading).
# W1 embeds this exact map and serves it for the IRI
#   https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/context/v1
# via the JSON-LD load callback; every other URL is refused.
#
# Vocabulary rule: a term is typed "@id" when its value is a pointer
# (edge target or resource locator), so it expands to an absolute IRI.
# Pointer value convention: vertex locals live under
#   https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/<local-name>
# repo-relative paths are encoded under
#   https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/path/<repo-path>   (strip the prefix -> path)
# so that every pointer is absolute up front and the compiler can map
# path pointers back to disk paths for resolution (C5).
